# Input
```md
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<!-- another leading comment -->

# Title

# Another top-level heading

```

# Diagnostics
```
html_comment_before_title.md:6:1 lint/nursery/useSingleTopLevelHeading ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i This document has more than one top-level heading.
  
    4 │ # Title
    5 │ 
  > 6 │ # Another top-level heading
      │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    7 │ 
  
  i The other top-level heading is here.
  
    2 │ <!-- another leading comment -->
    3 │ 
  > 4 │ # Title
      │ ^^^^^^^
    5 │ 
    6 │ # Another top-level heading
  
  i A single top-level heading acts as the document's title. Additional ones break document outlines, tables of contents, and the structure produced when converting to HTML.
  
  i Demote this heading to a lower level, or move its section into its own document.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```
